Description: implement zwp_keyboard_shortcuts_inhibit_manager_v1
 Native Wayland remote desktop clients such as OxuLnk ask the compositor to
 switch its keybindings off for their window. labwc 0.9.3 does not offer the
 protocol, so OxuLnk logs "keyboard grab unavailable: compositor does not
 support shortcut inhibition" and shows the grab as not working, although
 the image ships zero keybindings and every key already reaches it.
 .
 Adds src/protocols/keyboard-shortcuts-inhibit.c on top of the wlroots
 helper. Each inhibitor on a view's surface counts in a new per-view field,
 keybinds_inhibitors, which view_inhibits_actions() treats like the
 user-toggled inhibits_keybinds: keybindings are off while that view has the
 focus, and ToggleKeybinds still works as a way out. An inhibitor is
 activated once when it is created and never deactivated on a focus change,
 because clients read 'inactive' as "the user withdrew it" and do not ask
 again.
 .
 thinfloe-specific: not proposed for upstream inclusion, see Forwarded below.
Author: ThinFloe maintainers
Origin: vendor
Forwarded: not-needed
Last-Update: 2026-11-12
---
